<<ImagePlaceholder "Standing at the bathroom doorframe measuring her waist with twine" "portrait" "assets/characters/mc-female-phase1/d03-measuring.png">>

<div class="prose-block">

<p>I make a decision somewhere between the last bite of dry cereal and washing the bowl in the sink. Today is a research day. Clinical, methodical. I'm going to study this body the way I'd study for an exam, because that's the only framework I have that makes any sense right now.</p>

<p>Step one is measuring. I dig through the junk drawer in the kitchen and find a piece of twine left over from when I tried to hang a poster with no nails, and the ruler I used to mark margins on a homework assignment three months ago. These are the only measuring tools in the apartment. I work with what I have.</p>

<p>I strip down in front of the bathroom mirror, sports bra off, panties off, completely naked, goosebumps prickling across skin that's softer than it was three days ago. Softer than it has any right to be.</p>

<p>Height first. I stand against the doorframe where Marcus's pencil mark still sits at 5'9". I reach up and mark my own height with a fingernail scratch, step away, and hold the ruler against the frame.</p>

<p>Five foot six. Three inches shorter. Three inches of bone and cartilage and vertical space just gone overnight. I press my finger against Marcus's mark, then against mine. The gap between them is the distance between who I was and who I am.</p>

<p>Bust next. I wrap the twine around my chest at the fullest point, mark it with my thumb, lay it against the ruler. About thirty-four inches. I do it twice to be sure. Thirty-four.</p>

<p>Underbust, same process but under the breasts, around the ribcage. Twenty-seven inches. The difference between these two numbers is supposed to mean something about cup size, but I don't know what yet.</p>

<p>Waist, I feel for the narrowest point, which turns out to be above my navel, a dramatic inward curve Marcus's body never had. The string sits in a groove that feels carved. Twenty-four and a half inches.</p>

<p>Hips, the widest point, lower than I expected, mid-pelvis, where the bone flares out and then there's the added padding of flesh over it. I wrap the twine carefully, pulling it snug but not tight. Thirty-five and a half inches.</p>

</div>

<<ImagePlaceholder "A hand writing measurements on the back of a DashDrop receipt" "float" "assets/characters/mc-female-phase1/d03-measurements-note.png">>

<div class="prose-block">

<p>I write the numbers on the back of a DashDrop receipt with a pen that's running out of ink.</p>

<blockquote>Height: 5'6"<br>Bust: 34"<br>Underbust: 27"<br>Waist: 24.5"<br>Hips: 35.5"</blockquote>

<p>These are just numbers. They don't mean anything to me yet. But I'm going to find out.</p>

</div>

